    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d634">

                <pb facs="0794" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 863.852/202a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sammons</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-29T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 29, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You are authorized to sign charter parties vessels <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >China</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Silesia</hi> as agent United States
                    Shipping Board Emergency Fleet Corporation, and to have marine survey made.
                    Cable Department whether crews will be Chinese. Shipping Board plans employ
                    these vessels Pacific trade for North and South America for present, but desires
                    to make sure that no arrangement with crews prevents vessels being used North
                    Atlantic if desired.</p>
                <p>Department instructed Minister Reinsch by telegraph December 28<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d634-f1"/> to authorize you to sign charter parties <hi
                        rendition="#italic">China</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Silesia.</hi>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
